WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.097
Twenty-six billion dollars of Anthropic's

00:00:02.897 --> 00:00:04.610
record IPO came from the

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:06.426
companies that sell it chips

00:00:06.226 --> 00:00:07.031
and cloud.

00:00:07.731 --> 00:00:09.464
The record listing closed at

00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:11.252
about one hundred nineteen point

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:12.401
five billion dollars.

00:00:12.441 --> 00:00:14.510
The base deal alone beat

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.847
SpaceX as the largest IPO ever.

00:00:17.397 --> 00:00:19.504
Ninety-one point six billion went

00:00:19.304 --> 00:00:20.253
to Anthropic.

00:00:20.293 --> 00:00:22.424
The seven co-founders sold about

00:00:22.224 --> 00:00:23.138
two billion.

00:00:23.178 --> 00:00:25.739
Seven suppliers paid twenty-six billion

00:00:25.539 --> 00:00:26.989
for non-voting shares.

00:00:27.539 --> 00:00:29.355
Seven chip, memory and cloud

00:00:29.155 --> 00:00:30.970
companies bought those shares.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:33.336
Amazon, which already owned nearly

00:00:33.136 --> 00:00:35.462
fifteen percent, is notably absent.

00:00:36.012 --> 00:00:37.873
Shares were marketed at seventy

00:00:37.673 --> 00:00:39.718
to seventy-eight dollars and priced

00:00:39.518 --> 00:00:40.518
at eighty-three.

00:00:40.558 --> 00:00:42.073
Day one opened at one

00:00:41.873 --> 00:00:43.775
eleven fifty and closed up

00:00:43.575 --> 00:00:45.012
seventeen percent.

00:00:45.562 --> 00:00:47.392
Only about seven point four

00:00:47.192 --> 00:00:49.447
percent of shares trade freely,

00:00:49.247 --> 00:00:50.794
one analyst estimates.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.345
That thin float can swing

00:00:52.145 --> 00:00:53.656
the price hard either way.

00:00:54.206 --> 00:00:56.364
Anthropic expects to spend about

00:00:56.164 --> 00:00:58.253
nine hundred billion dollars on

00:00:58.053 --> 00:00:59.861
compute in the coming years.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:00.936
Much of it goes to

00:01:00.736 --> 00:01:02.486
the companies that just bought

00:01:02.286 --> 00:01:02.963
its stock.

00:01:03.513 --> 00:01:05.298
Claude's pricing is now tied

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.608
to quarterly earnings.

00:01:06.648 --> 00:01:08.953
Watch the first earnings report,

00:01:08.753 --> 00:01:10.777
pricing changes, and the day

00:01:10.577 --> 00:01:12.180
the insider lockup ends.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.659
Labs raise from chipmakers and

00:01:14.459 --> 00:01:16.521
clouds, then spend it with them.

00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:18.064
Now a public market sits

00:01:17.864 --> 00:01:19.367
in the middle of that loop.

